    "text": "TripVerse How it worksDestinationsExploreQuestionsSign in Start planning Agentic travel planningTripVerse works it out with you. Tell a guide where you are going and it drafts the days, keeps an eye on the budget, and opens the trip as a studio you can explore: a plan, a sketchbook, a map and a 3D route. Start planning Explore destinations Six guides. Pick who plans your trip with you. Seoul \u00b7 5 nightsPlanning now Read your brief Researched possible stops Checked your dates Writing your day-by-day draft Kyoto \u00b7 3 days \u00b7 budget Flights, Delhi and back~\u20b960,000 Stay, 2 nights~\u20b922,000 Activities~\u20b98,420 Food, 3 days~\u20b94,500 Local travel~\u20b93,600 ~\u20b998,520 suggested \u00b7 \u20b9150,000 budget Peak bloom \u00b7 early April14places across 3 days, each one movable by asking How it works01Say where you are goingTell your guide the place, or just the mood. It asks three quick things (where from, where to, how many days). Dates, budget, pace and interests are optional. 02Get a draft, or build it togetherGenerate the whole itinerary in one go, or plan one day at a time while your guide suggests places that fit the day and the budget. 03Open the Trip StudioOne page for the whole trip: the day plan, a hand-drawn sketchbook, a map, a 3D route, and the weather and public holidays for your dates. 04Change it by asking, then take it with youSay \u201cmove the market to day 1\u201d and it is done, with a receipt of what changed. Export a PDF, a calendar, map files or the budget as a spreadsheet. What the agent actually doesMost planners write you a list. This one keeps a plan you can change.Four things follow from that difference. Keep scrolling: this section moves sideways. Scroll Every change leaves a receipt01Ask for a change and it happensSay \u201cmove Nishiki Market to day 2\u201d and the plan changes, the studio follows, and a receipt under the reply lists exactly what changed. If a day gets too full or the budget is passed, it tells you instead of refusing. Drawn live, page by page02A guide who draws your tripPick a guide and they sketch each day on paper as the plan takes shape: the places, the order, the weather, the public holiday. Change something in the chat and the page is redrawn while you watch. Map and 3D in one studio03The itinerary is a map, not a listEvery stop sits on a real map and in a 3D route you can orbit, with photos, what is nearby, and the forecast or the season\u2019s typical weather for your dates. Suggested first, then yours to accept04A budget you can see, not guessSet a target in the brief, or just say it. The budget planner suggests typical costs from traveler reports, row by row, and nothing counts toward your total until you accept it. While it plansYour guide says what it is doing as it goes: researching stops, reading what travelers recommend, checking the weather and public holidays for your dates, then writing the days. The draft streams in, and the route draws itself alongside. WeatherA forecast near your dates, the month\u2019s typical beyond Traveler tipsLinked to the post they came from tripverse \u00b7 kyoto, 3 days YouPlan 3 days in Kyoto from Delhi. I love food and old temples. TripVerseI\u2019ve put together a balanced, three-day itinerary for your trip to Kyoto. Since you\u2019re traveling in mid-October, you\u2019ll be there during the pleasant autumn season, though October is part of the rainy season, so I\u2019ve built in some flexibility. Read your brief3 days \u00b7 2 travelers \u00b7 food, temples Researched possible stopsKyoto, from Delhi Checked your datesTypical for October \u00b7 Sports Day on day 1 Writing your day-by-day draftDay 2 of 3 Drawing the sketchbookQueued Day Planned Date Places D1 Fushimi Inari Taisha, Takashimaya food hall Mon 12 Oct, holiday 2 D2 Arashiyama Bamboo Grove, Kiyomizu-dera, Nishiki Market Tue 13 Oct 8 D3 Okochi-sanso Villa, Nishijin, Uji Wed 14 Oct 4 Places to start Explore destinations KyotoUKY Temple districts, kaiseki, autumn maples 4 nightsJapan PortoOPO Douro riverfront, tiled facades, port cellars 3 nightsPortugal PraguePRG Old Town rooftops, Vltava crossings 3 nightsCzechia SeoulICN Palace grounds, night markets, Bukchon 5 nightsSouth Korea BudapestBUD Thermal baths, Buda hill, ruin bars 3 nightsHungary SydneySYD Harbour walks, coastal track, ferries 6 nightsAustralia THE SOUVENIR YOU KEEPKeep the feeling. Turn the page. The views, the wrong turns, the people. A little journal for the things that made the trip. Made of moments. Meant to be opened. THE MEMORY STACKPHOTOGRAPHS, DETOURS & LITTLE THINGS Journal8 chapters \u00b7 a few favorite memories FIELD NOTES / THE MOUNTAINSSomewhere, slower. a little moment worth keepingNo alarms. No hurry. Just a little mountain air and a road we hadn\u2019t taken before. 01 / 08 01 / 08 Somewhere, slower. Swipe or use \u2190 \u2192 THE FIELD JOURNALPHOTOGRAPHS, DETOURS & LITTLE THINGS A JOURNAL OF LITTLE ESCAPESSomewhere, slower.the mountainsNo alarms. No hurry. Just a little mountain air and a road we hadn\u2019t taken before. 01 COLLECTED ALONG THE WAY / 01a different way of seeingless scrolling, more stories. 02 01 / 08 Somewhere, slower. Swipe or use \u2190 \u2192 A FEW PAGES FROM THE WORLD OUTSIDE.Leave a little room for the unexpected. Questions Plan the whole trip, not the paragraph about it. Start planning ProductHow it works Explore destinations Plan a trip Destinations Your tripsMy trips Sign in Create an account HelpHow to use TripVerse What the agent does Questions How was your experience?A quick reaction or a few words help us make TripVerse better. Rate your experienceRoughMehOkayHappyLoved it Anything you\u2019d like us to know? (optional)Send feedback \u00a9 2026 TripVerseBuilt with LangGraph, React Three Fiber, and FastAPICredits",
